# MicrobatchPort-1b (rebased onto stack/prx-fixed: the final rows of base6 split between the halves; the
# side wait inside prompt_shard_rows; PRX's zero-copy partials pass through HcSplit._post as before). MicrobatchPort-1: a row-split prompt chunk in two halves, one half's exchanges and glue under the other half's compute
# (TF_GLM_PROMPT_MICROBATCH=1 with TF_GLM_HC_SPLIT=1; default off until measured on the GB10 triangle).
#
# - Why: the row split's exchanges (every rank's fp32 partials of the other ranks' rows at two sites a layer, then the
#   glued rows) run on a side stream, but the main stream soon waits for them: the glue needs the partials, the next
#   block the glued rows. At three ranks a 4,096-row chunk moves ~32 MiB a peer each way at each of 90 sites
#   (HuntComms). Here half A = rows [0, h), half B = rows [h, R) (h a multiple of 192 at three ranks: 1,920 + 2,176
#   for a 4,096-row chunk), each row-split by its own HcSplit over row views of the prompt buffers on the one side
#   stream; per layer the main stream runs A's block, B's block, A's MoE, B's MoE, and after each a half's chain
#   (partial exchange, glue on own rows, row swap: HcSplit.glue_side) is queued on the side stream, joined only before
#   that half's next block.
# - microbatch.py (new): cut, applies, view, Halves, layer_steps.
# - hcsplit.py: SplitSettings.microbatch / micro_min (TF_GLM_PROMPT_MICROBATCH_MIN_ROWS, default 1,920) and
#   prompt_code (the ranks' startup comparison; not in code(), which keys the spill tier: the bits are the same);
#   HcSplit(stream=...), glue_side / join / drain, finish() draining a halved chunk's splits at a layer-sliced yield.
# - forward.py: split_layer_steps hands a qualifying chunk to microbatch; OTS 0101's prompt indexer shard gets the
#   half's side stream (_micro_side).
# - indexer_shard.py: prompt_shard(side=...): its main-stream all-gather waits for the side stream and the side stream
#   for it, so two collectives never run at once on a rank (as KV sharding's fetch already does).
# - engine.py: micro_code in the startup comparison and its message.
# - Not halved: multi-prompt chunks (multi_prefill), chunks off the 64-token grid, TF_GLM_KV_SHARD, TF_GLM_LATENT=0,
#   halves under the minimum, and a chunk whose OTS 0121 kept point falls in half A or at the cut.
#
# Bits: bit-identical. Each half is a chunk of the 64-token grid; every row's arithmetic is chunk-invariant there
# (chunkinv), both halves use the whole chunk's nch and head block, partial sums keep rank order (OTS 0105's rotation
# included), B's KDA continues from A's state and B's attention reads A's caches of the layer. Test:
